# m10_dead_boot_keys_release: free the last-loaded bootstrap phase keys at the end of every bootstrap.
# Position 10 on m9_ct_capacity_shrink; rule 4 against m9's peak table (122.8 GiB, 128,774,692 kB;
# zen4, 16-core cpuset, shared node, pmsample_chain; run m10r_dead_boot_keys_release).
#
# impl_lever: patch_dead_boot_keys_release.py
# impl_base_image: image:moai-cpu-m9_ct_capacity_shrink.sif
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: stage_load_boot_phase
# object_skipped: sealpool:retained
# object_skipped: all_layer_test()  <- keygenerator.h:208
# object_skipped: all_layer_test()  <- seal::Ciphertext::operator=
# object_skipped: stage_bootstrap_chunked  <- seal::Serialization::Load
# cost_class: free
# evidence: equivalent
# plaintext_equivalence: impl/equiv_layer_outputs.py
# not_selectable_until: m8_chunked_bootstrap
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# table      m9's peak (122.8 GiB, Layer-0 FFN window after the intermediate; by allocation site):
#              51.7 GB  38.5%  sealpool:retained   (the freed FFN intermediate's blocks, kept by the allocator; knob)
#              17.2 GB  12.8%  all_layer_test() (test_full_scheme.hpp:939)  <- keygenerator.h:208:create_galois_keys   (attention keys, Layer 0: needed by Layer 1; paid fix = park)
#              16.9 GB  12.6%  all_layer_test() (test_full_scheme.hpp:1340)  <- seal::Ciphertext::operator=   (boot_layer, live until the second residual add)
#              16.9 GB  12.6%  stage_bootstrap_chunked (test_full_scheme.hpp:807)  <- seal::Serialization::Load   (rtn, the FFN input, live)
#              14.5 GB  10.8%  stage_load_boot_phase (test_full_scheme.hpp:557)  <- kswitchkeys.h:239:seal::KSwitchKeys::load   (the last phase's bootstrap keys, DEAD: bootstrap2 is over, bootstrap3 loads its own)
#               6.5 GB   4.8%  gelu_v2  <- seal::Ciphertext::operator=
#               3.5 GB   2.6%  all_layer_test()  <- context.h:496:seal::SEALContext::SEALContext
# choice     above the row: pool aggregate (knob), attention keys (live for Layer 1), boot_layer and rtn
#            (live). Last-phase keys stay loaded after bootstrap2 until bootstrap3 replaces them (softmax
#            bootstrap likewise between heads). Freed at the end of each bootstrap. Same bytes, free.
#            Expected: FFN window -14.5 GB, peak stays there (~107).
# enabler    m7's peak rank 1 was the bootstrap working set; paid chunking (m8) exposed these windows.
# gate       bit-identical to m7 (md5 dc043a0b); equivalent to m0 through m6.
# RESULT (measured): peak 128,774,692 -> 113,618,040 kB (122.8 -> 108.4 GiB, -11.77%), wall 127,562 s, gate md5 dc043a0b. New peak: Layer-0 FFN window after gelu (after_gelu marker, 108.4 GiB; sealpool:retained 50.7 GB holds the released FFN intermediate).
# REFUTED IF the peak moves less than this system's run-to-run spread (2.0 pp), or the LEVER|dead_boot_keys_release markers are absent from markers.txt.
